<c.HEAD>"            &lt;p&gt;Eight sovereign narrators are the &lt;b&gt;base&lt;/b&gt; — each at once a &lt;b&gt;sun&lt;/b&gt; (it pulls) and a &lt;b&gt;planet&lt;/b&gt; (it orbits), glowing with the &lt;b&gt;f-mean of the hues it holds&lt;/b&gt;: the colour of its combination. Their centre of mass, the f-mean of the eight, is the global base; the 144 colour-name agents are the field it holds and sways. The constellation has a &lt;b&gt;point of view&lt;/b&gt; — turn the observer and the colour order holds; flip to the other side and it reverses. Same stars, read the other way.&lt;/p&gt;"</c>

